# Markdown conventions

Follow [markdownlint](https://github.com/DavidAnson/markdownlint) rules enforced in `.markdownlint.json`:

- **MD022** — Blank line before and after every heading.
- **MD031** — Blank line before and after fenced code blocks.
- **MD032** — Blank line before and after lists (and between a heading/paragraph and a list).
- **MD040** — Every fenced block must declare a language (`javascript`, `bash`, `html`, `text`, etc.). Use `text` for ASCII diagrams and directory trees.
- **MD024** — Do not repeat the same heading text within a file; vary wording or merge sections.
- **MD013** — Line length should be no more than 120 characters; wrap them if necessary.
- **MD026** — Headings must not end with `.`, `,`, `;`, `:`, `!`, or `?`.
- **MD060** — Table columns use any pipe alignment (pad or compact, but stay consistent per table).

Also prefer `[label](url)` over bare URLs when a link appears in prose.
